&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Legal Counsel, EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Legal Counsel (EMEA) based in the UK with deep SaaS commercial transaction experience to join our collaborative, forward-thinking legal team. At New Relic, legal isn’t just a support function, you will sit directly at the deal table, driving revenue growth, optimising customer and partner relationships, and scaling our SaaS business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will enjoy direct visibility, genuine autonomy, and the platform to curate your own career trajectory within a globally dispersed team. If you thrive in a dynamic environment, enjoy solving complex commercial challenges, and want to directly power our go-to-market strategy, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structure &amp;amp; Close SaaS Deals:&lt;/strong&gt; Draft, review, and negotiate complex SaaS agreements, including data processing addenda and security terms in direct support of EMEA go-to-market efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower Sales Teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Coach and advise regional sales teams on SaaS deal structure, negotiation tactics, and customer dispute resolution to accelerate sales velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale Channel Partnerships:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Partner business teams to structure, negotiate, and expand business via resellers, MSPs, distributors, and global system integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Privacy &amp;amp; Regulatory Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with Privacy Legal to embed practical risk-tolerance strategies and standardise commercial contract responses under global privacy regimes (GDPR, DORA, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Scalable Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Own, refine, and modernise SaaS agreement templates, negotiation playbooks, and contract escalation workflows to ensure legal scales alongside business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as a Trusted Advisor:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide pragmatic, risk-aware legal guidance across cross-functional partners, including Marketing, Product, Finance, and Contract Managers, aligning legal strategy with our consumption-based model, monetisation, and product-led growth (PLG) goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mandatory SaaS Commercial Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Substantial experience drafting and negotiating complex SaaS commercial contracts, partner frameworks, and cloud technology agreements with a solid knowledge of revenue recognition principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational &amp;amp; Qualification Background (UK): &lt;/strong&gt;Qualified to practice law and in good standing with the relevant professional regulatory body (e.g., state bar, Solicitors Regulation Authority, or equivalent) in your jurisdiction of residence&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy &amp;amp; Security Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid hands-on knowledge of data privacy, artificial intelligence, security topics, and global compliance frameworks within commercial SaaS transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM &amp;amp; Sales Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive, strategic approach to working directly alongside enterprise sales teams to drive deal execution across the EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to manage competing deliverables, set clear boundaries, prioritise under deadlines, and operate independently in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Outstanding interpersonal skills with a track record of building trust across functions, regions, and executive levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house legal experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with consumption-based in SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience handling GSI/Reseller partner agreements and advising marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An eagerness to leverage AI, with a deep understanding of AI products, LLMs and the product lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Privacy certifications (e.g., CIPP/E) or deep familiarity with the EU AI Act and DORA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
